  "publication_text": {
    "summary": "The universal nonmembership conjecture in Karpenko's 2016 Oberwolfach contribution is false at n=8. There is a 17-dimensional quadratic form phi over a characteristic-zero field F with even Clifford index 256 such that, for K=F(SB(C0(phi))) and X=OG8(phi), the original distinguished class e8 belongs to gamma5 K(X_K). The note retains the original field, special class and maximal-index hypothesis. It gives a complete negative answer to the universal statement, without asserting failure for every n or exact filtration depth.",
    "priority_statement": "This is an exposition and independent explicit verification of a consequence of prior work. Karpenko's original pointwise transfer and filtration theorem, together with the previously computed Spin(18) index bound, already imply the conclusion. The index is printed in author versions dated May 2021, summarized with Merkurjev in 2022 and published in 2023. Karpenko's later analytic proof, in an August 2023 author version and the 2024 original/2025 translation, supplies the bound used in the main proof. No new Spin-index theorem or class-valuation theorem is claimed. Priority for an explicit earlier combined gamma-filtration statement and for the specific numerical witnesses remains unestablished; no firstness or current worldwide openness is claimed.",
    "verification_scope": "The supporting archive preserves the eight original submitted files and explicit authored mathematical/priority reviews, source-reading receipts, manuscript and finite verification programs. Four mathematical families used an analytic polynomial obstruction, an explicit maximal-index field model, and independent exact intersection computations. The pairing 14668659594398531584 equals 2^22 times 3497280977821; it independently verifies a previously published class valuation of 22. Only an index upper bound of 8 is needed. Standard published Clifford, filtration, transfer, Chow-ring and Gysin/localization theorems remain explicit dependencies. The corrected eight-factor normalization is 2^8, despite the Appendix A prose printing 2^3. Original historical records of computations not run in October 11 remain historical; current executable checks do not retroactively certify missing historical inputs or source-author Maple runs. Initial input/source receipts sometimes followed reading; recorded clock bounds and custody limits are disclosed. Third-party source bodies, provider responses, caches and raw scratch are omitted from the portable archive. Independent family inputs, later cross-review exposure and root tooling-only feedback are disclosed in the actual gates and seals. AI tools were used extensively in research, solving, verification, literature review, drafting and internal adversarial review. This work is unrefereed; no external human peer review, journal acceptance or formal proof-assistant certification is claimed."
  },
  "tracker": {
    "original_problem": "30003042 (OWR-14213-008): Karpenko's gamma-filtration nonmembership conjecture; https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/1271",
    "notes": "Complete negative answer at n=8: dimension17, even Clifford index256, original SB splitting field, e8 in gamma5. Credited consequence of prior Karpenko and related index/filtration results; later analytic proof and independently reproduced finite certificates. Priority unestablished; preprint and scoped verification archive."
  },
